{"id":108498,"vol":{"id":18058,"name":"Detective Comics"},"num":"665","name":"Lightning Changes","title":"Detective Comics #665","year":"1993","date":"1993-08-31","store":"","poster":"https://comicvine.gamespot.com/a/uploads/scale_medium/11112/111120209/5511555-detective%20comics%20%23665.jpg","big":"https://comicvine.gamespot.com/a/uploads/scale_large/11112/111120209/5511555-detective%20comics%20%23665.jpg","pub":"DC Comics","deck":"","desc":"Batman continues to be on the mend, and Jean-Paul is standing in for the great Detective. Jean-Paul allows himself to be drawn into the persona of the Batman and begins to loose his concept of justice. Robin is torn between letting Bruce know, or stay with Jean-Paul to keep him from getting killed. Neither Bruce Wayne or Jean-Paul Valley are getting what either expect, and Robin is on the wire.\n\nNotes:","people":[{"id":30188,"name":"Adrienne Roy","role":"colorist"},{"id":41486,"name":"Chuck Dixon","role":"writer"},{"id":5584,"name":"Dick Giordano","role":"inker"},{"id":3244,"name":"Graham Nolan","role":"penciler"},{"id":9421,"name":"John Costanza","role":"letterer"},{"id":7063,"name":"Kelley Jones","role":"penciler, inker, cover"},{"id":43254,"name":"Scott J. Peterson","role":"editor"}],"chars":[{"id":1699,"name":"Batman","image":"https://comicvine.gamespot.com/a/uploads/scale_small/11144/111442876/8759934-jrjrhr.jpg"},{"id":5556,"name":"Alfred Pennyworth","image":"https://comicvine.gamespot.com/a/uploads/scale_small/12/124259/8057339-e2lokwbxsaazhqn.jpg"},{"id":9290,"name":"Tim Drake","image":"https://comicvine.gamespot.com/a/uploads/scale_small/11156/111564182/9852320-tdrakeb01.jpg"}],"arcs":[{"id":40761,"name":"\"Batman\" Knightfall"}]}